{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01HHykVC2ALDp27Nm8MtxwoS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. Wrote `ai-engineering/answers/07-003-how-reduce-latency-in-genai-applications.md` — the Q3 answer on reducing latency in GenAI applications.\n\n**Key content in the note:**\n- **TTFT vs total latency** distinction — prefill is compute-bound (scales with input tokens), decode is memory-bandwidth-bound; they need different fixes\n- **5-layer stack** in ROI order:\n  1. Semantic cache (cosine > 0.93 → < 10 ms, 20–35% hit rate)\n  2. Streaming SSE (perceived TTFT fix, zero structural cost — always add this first for user-facing features)\n  3. Prompt compression + top-3 reranking (60% token reduction → proportional prefill speedup)\n  4. Model tiering (GPT-4o-mini ~3–4× faster, handle 60%+ of FAQ traffic)\n  5. vLLM PagedAttention + speculative decoding (self-hosted; 2–4× decode speedup on structured outputs)\n- **Before/after table**: baseline 2400 ms p95 → 550 ms blended after all layers\n- **Concrete pitfall**: treating TTFT and total latency as the same thing, and adding streaming as an afterthought rather than step one"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":279,"cache_read_input_tokens":75521,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":279,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7dc9eeb8-f0bc-4ad9-9337-a0a3895a39e4","uuid":"899df560-d751-4673-8267-3f169b1f890f"}
